A whole bunch of stuff happened, so I'll try to explain all the new characters, and what's going on.

00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:11.140
Especially with the big twist at the end  (the big post-credits scene).

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:14.900
This is prob'ly going to be the closest we'll ever get to a musical episode.

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:20.518
A lot of the main cast members have musical backgrounds either on television or as actual musical artists.

00:00:20.518 --> 00:00:23.498
Stephen Amell has the funniest answers when people ask them if they're ever going to do

00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.500
a musical episode of Arrow.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.580
His answers are usually along the lines of:

00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:27.360
 "Never" 

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:29.040
and, "Over my dead body".

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:30.860
Okay, so just careful for spoilers from the episode.

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:35.440
I'm gonna start with Explainers for the characters that we just met in the episode (like the brand new characters).

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:36.900
First up is "Peek-a-Boo".

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.440
She's actually a character that Geoff Johns created in the comics.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.880
Her origin is pretty close to what it is in the comics, as well as what her character does.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.060
She has a boyfriend who's in prison.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.360
She helps him break out.

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.220
And he convinces her to use her ability to steal money.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.540
She's one of those characters that's relatively new, and doesn't get used a lot. 

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:57.920
So she doesn't have the long history that a lot of the other Rogues like Captain Cold and Heat Wave have.

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.620
She IS really useful for teeing up the idea of 'toxic relationships'.

00:01:01.900 --> 00:01:04.780
She's still in love with Clay Parker -- prob'ly needs to get over him.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.140
Caitlin Snow: 

00:01:06.140 --> 00:01:09.040
Still in love with Ronnie Raymond -- prob'ly needs to get over him.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:14.640
I always talk about narrative symmetry, so, think about what's going on with Peek-a-Boo's relationship

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:19.680
and what it might say about the future of Caitlin Snow and the 'Firestorm' relationship (how that might develop).

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.380
Caitlin's prob'ly gonna get "raked over the coal", so to speak.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.960
Next up on the list, is Linda Park.

00:01:25.160 --> 00:01:29.960
In the comics, she's mostly known as the wife of Wally West (of the Wally West Flash).

00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:32.380
Obviously the shows playing with the timeline just a little bit.

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.000
They ARE going to do the Wally West at some point, but it's gonna be closer to The New⁵² Wally West.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.380
He'll be an African-American. 

00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.080
And just because she's going out with Barry now doesn't mean she won't ultimately get married to Wally West in the future.

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:45.940
If you didn't recognize her, the actress playing her is Malese Jow.

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.700
I feel like she did a really good job.

00:01:47.892 --> 00:01:51.892
She was really only a small part of this episode, but we're gonna see her more in the next couple of episodes.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.720
Like, they'll develop that character.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:59.459
She 'n Iris West can totally duke it out as to which female, Flash-family-member, gets Speed Force powers first.

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:05.120
Yes, there have been times in the comics when Iris West, and Linda Park, have had Speed Force powers.

00:02:05.120 --> 00:02:09.480
I don't think they're gonna do anything close to that this season, but, just keep that in the back of your mind.

00:02:09.480 --> 00:02:12.400
It is possible that we could get a female speedster at some point.

00:02:12.920 --> 00:02:15.220
Then obviously the last big introduction is, "Gorilla Grodd"

00:02:15.220 --> 00:02:17.260
Like FULL ON Gorilla Grodd.

00:02:17.560 --> 00:02:20.940
I've already done an Explainer video for him, so I'll just add a link in the description.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.218
Basically, they are bringing him on: full steam ahead.

00:02:24.218 --> 00:02:29.078
Really what you need to know, is that Gorilla Grodd, in the comics, ...is fairly evil.

00:02:29.080 --> 00:02:31.780
So he'll be one of the more angry villains that we'll see on the show.

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:32.280
Okay.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.660
So moving on to Top 5 Moments.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:37.220
No. 5: The Flash is learning to use his abilities in new ways.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.760
Like they said in the beginning, "He's getting faster" 

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.140
Progressively* faster.

00:02:41.140 --> 00:02:44.300
And he's learning new ways to use his Speed Force power to help people.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:46.840
Him vibrating his hands on the door to open it? 

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.620
That's going to be a precursor to him, you know, flat-out vibrating through walls.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.300
I DO think we'll see that this season.

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:55.689
If we're going to see time travel, we'll prob'ly see him phase through a wall.

00:02:55.689 --> 00:02:57.429
For those that haven't seen any of the news: 

00:02:57.429 --> 00:02:59.289
They've been pretty open about the time travel stuff.

00:02:59.289 --> 00:03:00.909
I think that's Episode 17.

00:03:00.909 --> 00:03:03.860
It's the first episode that the new "Weather Wizard" is gonna be in.

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:06.410
It'll be like an 'accidental time travel' situation.

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:08.960
I'll talk more about it whenever that episode gets here.

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.420
Moving on to No. 4: Barry's dad does some detective work.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:16.800
The really cool thing about John Wesley Shipp helping out in the episode, is that it means that he might

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:21.540
be able to get more scenes in future episodes (or future seasons) inside the prison.

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:25.260
It gives his character more places to go, and it gave them some really nice scenes.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.980
"If my son were the Flash, I'd be really proud of him"

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.140
I know everyone's hoping that he'll secretly turn out to be Jay Garrick, or something like that.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:36.200
They could totally do some weird storyline where he gets temporary Speed Force powers. 

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:37.580
But that's kind of outlandish.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.560
I think his storyline will be more of this:

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:43.360
Until they clear him of the murder, he's going to have more 'prison break' scenes.~

00:03:43.420 --> 00:03:45.200
Make as many jokes about that as you want.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:48.620
This episode in general just ended up turning into kind of a Prison Break episode.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.700
Pied Piper broke out of prison.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:53.580
Peek-a-Boo broke her boyfriend, Clay Parker, out of prison.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:55.140
That's gonna happen more and more.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.940
The more people they lock up -- the more people will escape.

00:03:58.300 --> 00:03:59.500
Which is actually a nice intro to

00:03:59.500 --> 00:04:02.680
 No. 3: Pied Piper explains "Firestorm".

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:05.680
There are actually a couple things going on with this Pied Piper storyline.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.780
One: He got away. 

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:08.900
Which means he could show up in a future episode.

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:13.440
What I'm hoping for is that they'll do something close to the 1ˢᵗ appearance of Gorilla Grodd in the comics.

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.540
Grodd goes on a rampage in the city. 

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:17.820
Pied Piper helps Team Flash take him down.

00:04:18.217 --> 00:04:21.037
Hartley's been kind of a dick so far, so I don't know if he's gonna help 'em out.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:24.099
But it would be really cool to see him in that Gorilla Grodd episode.

00:04:24.099 --> 00:04:26.831
As he said though, he totally held up his end of the bargain.

00:04:26.831 --> 00:04:31.269
They see footage of what happened to Ronnie Raymond, and Professor Martin Stein.

00:04:31.269 --> 00:04:33.420
I like that freaky looking shot of Robbie Amell's face.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.660
...it just looks so scary.

00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.660
They kind of explained it in the post credits scene. 

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:41.360
The next episode is gonna be them trying to separate Ronnie, from Professor Martin Stein. 

00:04:41.360 --> 00:04:44.180
They're trying to like, "deactivate" Firestorm (so to speak). 

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.480
Moving on to No. 2: 'Snowbarry' karaoke night. 

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:50.734
Like I said, probably the closest we'll ever get to a musical episode.

00:04:50.734 --> 00:04:54.560
 I'm not really big on stuff like that, but I love it when they can have fun for just a few minutes.

00:04:54.560 --> 00:04:58.260
If you're not familiar with it, they were singing the song from Grease, " Summer Lovin'"

00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.940
They're both tryin' to find new relationships.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:05.600
And I THINK what's developing, at least what I saw, is sort of a reverse Ollicity situation. 

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.560
Told from the female's perspective.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.220
So if you're not familiar with Ollicity: 

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:13.660
You have Oliver Queen, in love with Felicity, but can't be with her.

00:05:14.020 --> 00:05:17.580
Per Stephen Amell's explanation, she is, "unattainable".

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:18.960
It's just like an unattainable thing.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.080
It's never gonna happen.

00:05:20.080 --> 00:05:21.880
At least the way that the Fandom wants it to.

00:05:22.120 --> 00:05:22.620
So

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.800
I think the same situation is gonna develop between Barry, and Caitlin Snow.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:30.500
She'll develop those, 'Ollicity' type-feelings for Barry.

00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:34.089
The look on her face at the end (whenever she was thinking about it), that's what sold me on it.

00:05:34.089 --> 00:05:38.633
Just think of the emotional havoc that's gonna wreak whenever Firestorm comes back into the narrative.

00:05:38.633 --> 00:05:41.184
'Cause there will be a ton of Firestorm in the back-half of the season.

00:05:41.184 --> 00:05:42.760
You guys can let me know what you think, but:  

00:05:42.760 --> 00:05:45.680
Is it Barry, that she is developing feelings for?

00:05:45.884 --> 00:05:48.104
