00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:33.560
I was scanning my Twitter feed for news, and I saw that Greg Burlanti tweeted, 

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.800
"Be sure you watch tonight's Flash, if you like giant gorillas"

00:06:37.040 --> 00:06:38.560
And I was just like, "wait...what?"

00:06:38.560 --> 00:06:45.180
I can't remember off the top of my head---it might be Ep isode 14 or 15---but Grodd will be in a full-on episode.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.740
In broad daylight, running around, being crazy.

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:51.600
Based on the special effects in this episode, it makes me really hopeful for the future of the series.

00:06:51.600 --> 00:06:55.340
If they can do special effects like this (on the cheap), and it looks this good,

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:58.580
then that means they'll be able to do all kinds of crazy superpowers.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.140
Here's my big question for you guys:

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:05.120
Given what they've done with Gorilla Grodd so far, where would you like to see them take that character?

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:09.080
So while you guys think about that, just to talk about some of the Easter Eggs that I haven't already mentioned.

